# GeT-RM reference material, Coriell ID HG01359 (Colombian in Medellin,
# Colombia, 1000 Genomes). GeT-RM consensus diplotype: *1/*4 (2/2 labs
# tested agreeing). Source: Pratt VM et al., "Characterization of
# Reference Materials for TPMT and NUDT15: A GeT-RM Collaborative
# Project." J Mol Diagn 2022;24:1079-1088 (PMID 35850928), Table 2, as
# reproduced in CDC's public-domain data table
# (https://www.cdc.gov/lab-quality/media/pdfs/2024/08/TPMT-and-NUDT15-reference-materials_508C.pdf,
# retrieved 2026-08-19). Genotype below constructed from this project's own
# dbSNP-confirmed defining-variant coordinate (genes/nudt15.py), not
# redistributed from GeT-RM/Coriell/CDC directly.
#
# A second, differently-shaped real limitation this module's scope
# exposes, not constructed to be interesting: NUDT15 *4 is an
# uncertain/unknown-function allele (genes/nudt15.py's module docstring)
# that does not carry the R139C substitution this module checks -- so, like
# *5 in NA19079.vcf/HG00437.vcf, it is entirely invisible to this module.
# Presented with this genotype, this module sees homozygous reference at
# the one position it checks and reports *1/*1, Normal Metabolizer. Per
# CPIC's Table 1, the true consensus phenotype for *1/*4 is Indeterminate
# (one normal function allele PLUS one uncertain/unknown function allele),
# NOT Normal Metabolizer -- a real, more concerning miscall than
# NA19079.vcf's undercalled-severity case, since it reports unwarranted
# confidence (a specific Normal Metabolizer conclusion) rather than
# flagging genuine uncertainty. Documented plainly, not glossed over -- see
# docs/VALIDATION.md.
#CHROM	POS	ID	REF	ALT	QUAL	FILTER	INFO	FORMAT	SAMPLE1
chr13	48045719	rs116855232	C	T	99	PASS	.	GT	0/0
